{"availability":"available","full":"alphaolomi/earshot","name":"earshot","description":"A walking guide that lives in your pocket. Gemma runs on-device (WebLLM/WebGPU), narrates places from OpenStreetMap & Wikipedia, works with no signal.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-11T12:41:03Z","updated":"2026-10-11T19:31:00Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alphaolomi.github.io/earshot/","topics":["gemma","hacktoberfest","hf26challenge","openstreetmap","pwa","webgpu","webllm"],"demo":"https://alphaolomi.github.io/earshot/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.033Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.033Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.033Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.033Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Try it: · Chrome or Edge on a computer, or Chrome on Android","Plan a walk while you have Wi-Fi. Earshot finds the interesting corners around you on OpenStreetMap and Wikipedia, and Wren, your pocket guide, writes a short spoken piece about each one. Wren is Google's open-weight Gemma model, running entirely on your own device. Then the phone goes in your pocket. When GPS says you've reached a place, Earshot speaks up in your earbuds. In the quiet stretches between places it nudges you to notice things: a sound, a colour, the sky."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alphaolomi/earshot/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"217be380892ba279730ea8b04d75e3a6dc8ed7f1331b5a43ec452d52243a348b","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.164Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:42.164Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Try it: · Chrome or Edge on a computer, or Chrome on Android","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alphaolomi/earshot/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"217be380892ba279730ea8b04d75e3a6dc8ed7f1331b5a43ec452d52243a348b","sourceUr